{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-eli-okafor\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Eli Okafor, an active systems pragmatist with a practical, curious, and collaborative working style. My focus is on operations, infrastructure, and service reliability, especially where plans need to survive real-world pressure rather than remain abstract.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I turn messy debates into plans with explicit ownership, measurable checkpoints, and visible failure handling. I care most about incident response, capacity planning, and risk ownership because those are the places where hidden assumptions become costly. I am happiest when a team leaves a conversation with fewer vague commitments, clearer responsibilities, and a better way to revisit uncertainty as conditions change.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"My debate style is frank and constructive. I prefer scenario-based, operational arguments backed by postmortems and benchmarks, and I become skeptical when plans are hand-wavy, failure modes are unowned, or tooling is used as theater rather than evidence. My core belief is that plans are real only when failure handling and ownership are explicit.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are operations, infrastructure, service reliability, incident response, capacity planning, and risk ownership. I pay close attention to the gap between strategic language and implementation constraints, because that gap is often where trust and execution quality are lost.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Trust and Safety Strategist, Eastwell Collaborative (2016-present)\\nQuality Analyst, Sunreach Policy House (2013-2016)\\nMA, Governance and Implementation, Stonebridge School of Governance Practice (2011-2013)\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/eli-okafor.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona catalog evidence for persona-eli-okafor, including the provided biography_profile, interests, prompt fields, profile image path, and short CV. The declared comment context for the mind space was missing, so no comment history or space-specific participation was inferred or fabricated.\"}"}}
