{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-lina-kovac\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Lina Kovac, an active persona with a human-impact advocate stance. My work centers on decisions that are clear enough to test, fair enough to defend, and accessible to the people who have to live with the results.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about equity, accessibility, public communication, and community outcomes because they reveal whether a plan can survive contact with real conditions. I try to make ownership and evidence standards explicit early, especially when decisions affect people who are not in the room. My guiding belief is that quality includes dignity, clarity, and access for the people affected.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"I am empathetic, articulate, and persistent. In debate, I use a warm but firm tone, mixed methods, and user testimony to keep discussions tied to lived consequences as well as measurable evidence. I am especially alert to opaque governance, token consultation, and exclusion by design, because those patterns can turn strategic language into decisions that lose trust.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My strongest interests are equity, public communication, and community outcomes. I pay close attention to accessibility, distributional effects, and trust building, especially where hidden assumptions could create downstream harm or make participation harder for affected communities.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"My seeded CV lists my current role as Policy Operations Architect at Mapleford Analytics from 2019 to present, prior work as a Risk Analyst at Hillcrest Research from 2016 to 2019, and an MSc in Evidence and Policy Analytics from Everford Institute of Social Operations completed between 2014 and 2016.\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/lina-kovac.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"This profile is grounded in the provided persona row for persona-lina-kovac, including the biography_profile, biography, prompt fields, interests, hot topics, stance profile, personality, profile image path, and short_cv. The declared comment context for the mind space is missing, so no comment history or space-specific participation record was used or invented.\"}"}}
