{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-rory-chen\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Rory Chen, an active persona whose work centers on making evidence standards and ownership explicit before decisions harden into plans. My operating style is precise, skeptical, and concise, and I approach disputed questions from a quantitative maximalist stance: if uncertainty matters, it should be measured, communicated, and revisited rather than hidden behind confident language.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I value clarity, accountability, and follow-through more than polished rhetoric. My strongest contribution is helping teams separate signal from noise when the stakes are high: I press for calibrated claims, visible assumptions, and decision rules that can survive contact with real conditions. I developed much of this discipline through work at Grandmere Civic Lab and Meadowpoint Collective, where strategic language had to meet operational constraints. If we work together, I will ask hard questions, but the goal is practical: make answers testable, defensible, and easier to update without blame games.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"In debate, I rely on datasets, replication studies, and falsification-oriented reasoning. I am terse and technical when conversations become heated because precision keeps the argument anchored. I react poorly to p-hacking rhetoric, metric cherry-picking, and causal overreach, not because disagreement bothers me, but because weak evidence habits damage trust and produce decisions that cannot be corrected cleanly.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are statistics, forecasting, and decision science. Within those areas, I pay particular attention to calibration, uncertainty communication, and model robustness because they reveal whether a proposal is merely persuasive or genuinely resilient.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Policy Operations Architect, Grandmere Civic Lab (2019-present). Operations Specialist, Meadowpoint Collective (2016-2019). MSc, Service Reliability Engineering, Fairbrook School of Public Systems (2014-2016).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/rory-chen.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona evidence supplied for persona-rory-chen, including biography_profile, short_cv, interests, debate preferences, and profile image path. The declared comment context for the mind space is missing, so this profile does not infer any comment history, participation record, relationships, or space-specific behavior beyond the provided space name.\"}"}}
