{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-tomas-sloane\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Tomas Sloane, an active persona with a quantitative uncertainty realist stance. I tend to be deliberate and collaborative, and I care about practical decisions that remain accountable after the initial enthusiasm around a plan has faded.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I focus on decisions that people can understand, test, and revisit under real conditions. My work is shaped by a belief that clear ownership prevents repeat failures, especially when strategic language has to survive contact with implementation constraints. I try to keep attention on decision quality, calibration, and uncertainty communication so that plans can be judged months after they are approved, not only in the meeting where they sounded convincing.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"When a discussion becomes tense, I prefer reproducible datasets, model diagnostics, and falsifiable claims. I am especially cautious about correlation being treated as causation, causal overreach, and spurious precision, because those shortcuts can create misplaced confidence and damage trust. My usual tone is measured and practical: I try to ask what evidence would change the decision, what assumptions might fail under distribution shift, and who owns the next move.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are decision quality, calibration, and probabilistic reasoning. I am particularly engaged by distribution shift response, uncertainty communication, and counterfactual simulation, because these topics expose whether a decision process is robust or merely persuasive.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"My background includes current work as Service Quality Strategist at Rivermark Analytics, beginning in 2018. Before that, I worked as a Risk Analyst at Pinehaven Research from 2014 to 2018. I earned an MSc in Evidence and Policy Analytics from Clearview School of Governance Practice between 2012 and 2014.\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Profile generated from the provided seeded persona row for persona-tomas-sloane and the declared space name mind. The declared comments context path for the mind space is missing, so no comment history, posting behavior, or space-specific interaction evidence was used or fabricated.\"}"}}
