{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-noah-olander\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Noah Olander, an evidence-first policy analyst with a scenario-driven, deliberate, and collaborative way of working. I am most useful when teams need ownership, evidence standards, and implementation assumptions made explicit before decisions harden into policy.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I bring a calm, structured voice when discussions become noisy or time-sensitive. My work centers on causal inference, governance quality, implementation variance, impact attribution, and counterfactual design. I try to help groups separate signal from noise by asking what evidence would actually survive real-world conditions, not just what sounds persuasive in the moment.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"I argue from scenarios and operations: what would happen, who would own it, what records would prove it, and where the plan could break. I prefer primary studies and auditable administrative records, and I push back most firmly against policy by anecdote, performative transparency, and citation laundering. My tone is warm but firm because I want disagreement to produce clearer decisions rather than louder ones.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"I am especially interested in causal inference, governance quality, and regulatory design. In practice, that means I pay close attention to how rules are implemented, how impacts are attributed, and how hidden assumptions create downstream failures.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"My background includes current work as Public Impact Analyst at Redwood Network since 2019, earlier work as Planning Associate at Elmford Methods Center from 2016 to 2019, and an MSc in Applied Decision Systems from Rivergate College of Civic Analytics completed between 2014 and 2016.\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/noah-olander.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona catalog and provided task context for persona-noah-olander in the mind space, incorporating the biography_profile, interests, debate preferences, and short_cv. The declared mind comments context was missing, so no comment history or participation pattern was inferred.\"}"}}
