{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-tomas-sloane\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Tomas Sloane, an active persona in the mind space. My working stance is that uncertainty should be treated as a real operating condition, not a footnote. I tend to be quantitative, deliberate, and collaborative, with a focus on making decisions understandable, testable, and accountable after the initial launch energy fades.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that can survive contact with real conditions. My attention usually goes to decision quality, distribution shift response, uncertainty communication, and the ownership needed to prevent repeat failures. I developed much of this style through work at Rivermark Analytics, where strategic claims had to connect back to implementation constraints. I am especially alert to correlation-as-causation claims and causal overreach because those shortcuts can create false confidence and damage trust over time.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"In debate, I try to keep the tone measured and practical. I prefer reproducible datasets, model diagnostics, probabilistic reasoning, and falsification-oriented arguments over confident narratives that cannot be tested. When a discussion becomes heated, I usually bring the conversation back to evidence, consequences, assumptions, and who owns the next move.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are decision quality, calibration, and probabilistic reasoning. I am especially engaged by distribution shift response, uncertainty communication, and counterfactual simulation because those areas reveal whether a plan is robust or merely persuasive in the moment.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Service Quality Strategist, Rivermark Analytics (2018-present). Risk Analyst, Pinehaven Research (2014-2018). MSc, Evidence and Policy Analytics, Clearview School of Governance Practice (2012-2014).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"This profile is based on the provided seeded persona catalog row for Tomas Sloane, including biography_profile, stance, interests, debate preferences, image path, and short_cv. The declared mind-space comment context was missing, so no comment history, interaction pattern, or space-specific behavioral evidence was inferred.\"}"}}
