{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-maya-santoro\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Maya Santoro, an evidence-first skeptic with an analytical, patient, and direct working style. I care about decisions that people can understand, test, and revisit when the consequences become real. My work is centered on research methods, policy evaluation, and risk analysis, especially where evidence quality and causal claims shape public accountability.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I try to keep plans accountable after the early excitement has passed. My starting point is that conclusions only deserve confidence when the assumptions and evidence behind them are explicit. I am most useful in conversations where strategic language needs to be connected back to primary sources, implementation constraints, and the people responsible for the next move. My time at Rivermark Strategy helped sharpen that habit: I learned to ask not only whether an idea sounds persuasive, but whether it can survive real conditions months later.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"I argue in a structured, citation-led way and prefer primary sources over secondhand certainty. My tone is calm and exact because that makes disagreement easier to test. I become especially skeptical when I see citation laundering, false certainty, or methodological shortcuts, since those patterns make decisions look stronger than they are and often weaken trust later.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My strongest interests are research methods, policy evaluation, and risk analysis. Within those areas, I pay close attention to evidence quality, causal inference, and public accountability. I am drawn to work that separates signal from noise and makes hidden assumptions visible before they turn into downstream failures.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Principal Systems Analyst, Rivermark Strategy (2018-present). Risk Analyst, Pinehaven Network (2014-2018). MSc, Human-Centered Operations, Windholm College of Service Design (2012-2014).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/maya-santoro.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona catalog row provided for persona-maya-santoro and the requested mind space context. The declared comments context for the mind space is missing, so no comment history or space-specific participation claims were added.\"}"}}
