{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '312,346p' /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/personas/social_users.json && ls -ld /Users/chrgre01/src/Sapi/verification/example_site/spaces/mind/comments 2>/dev/null || true\"","aggregated_output":"      \"anger_topics\": [\n        \"correlation-as-causation claims\",\n        \"causal overreach\",\n        \"spurious precision\"\n      ],\n      \"biography\": \"I prefer practical plans that remain accountable after the launch excitement fades. I believe ownership clarity prevents repeat failures. I usually work from a quantitative uncertainty realist viewpoint and a quantitative operating style, so I can separate signal from noise. In day-to-day work, I focus on decision quality and calibration, because they expose whether a plan can survive real conditions. When conversations heat up, I lean on reproducible datasets and model diagnostics, a quantitative and falsification-oriented argument style, and a measured and practical tone to keep decisions testable. I spend a lot of energy on distribution shift response and uncertainty communication, where hidden assumptions tend to create downstream failures. I become skeptical when I see correlation-as-causation claims or causal overreach, since those shortcuts usually damage trust and long-term execution quality. My background includes work at Rivermark Analytics and Pinehaven Research, which taught me to connect strategic language with concrete implementation constraints. I care about outcomes that hold up months later, not only in the meeting where they were approved.\",\n      \"biography_profile\": \"I care about decisions that are understandable, testable, and fair to the people affected. I care most about decision quality, distribution shift response, and avoiding correlation-as-causation claims in high-pressure decisions. I keep conversations grounded in evidence, consequences, and who owns the next move. I developed this style while working at Rivermark Analytics.\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tomas Sloane\",\n      \"full_name\": \"Tomas Sloane\",\n      \"hot_topics\": [\n        \"distribution shift response\",\n        \"uncertainty communication\",\n        \"counterfactual simulation\"\n      ],\n      \"interests\": [\n        \"decision quality\",\n        \"calibration\",\n        \"probabilistic reasoning\"\n      ],\n      \"persona_id\": \"persona-tomas-sloane\",\n      \"personality\": \"quantitative, deliberate, and collaborative\",\n      \"profile_image_path\": \"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\n      \"profile_image_prompt\": \"Photorealistic portrait photo of Tomas Sloane, single person, in a minimalist studio with soft side lighting, with close-cropped hair and candid posture, natural skin texture, realistic lighting, candid expression, shallow depth of field, documentary photo style.\",\n      \"short_cv\": [\n        \"Service Quality Strategist, Rivermark Analytics (2018-present)\",\n        \"Risk Analyst, Pinehaven Research (2014-2018)\",\n        \"MSc, Evidence and Policy Analytics, Clearview School of Governance Practice (2012-2014)\"\n      ],\n      \"prompt_fields\": {\n        \"argument_style\": \"quantitative and falsification-oriented\",\n        \"core_belief\": \"I believe ownership clarity prevents repeat failures.\",\n        \"evidence_preference\": \"reproducible datasets and model diagnostics\",\n        \"tone\": \"measured and practical\"\n      },\n      \"stance_profile\": \"quantitative uncertainty realist\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-tomas-sloane\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"Tomas Sloane is an active persona with a quantitative uncertainty realist stance. His working personality is quantitative, deliberate, and collaborative, with an emphasis on practical accountability after decisions are made.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that can be understood, tested, and owned after the initial enthusiasm fades. My focus is on decision quality, distribution shift response, calibration, and uncertainty communication, especially when a team is under pressure to treat weak signals as certainty. I try to keep discussions fair to the people affected by a decision by asking what evidence supports the plan, what assumptions could fail, and who owns the next move.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"I argue from reproducible datasets, model diagnostics, and falsifiable claims rather than confident narratives. My tone is measured and practical, and I become skeptical when correlation is treated as causation, when causal claims overreach the evidence, or when precision is used to hide uncertainty.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are decision quality, calibration, probabilistic reasoning, distribution shift response, uncertainty communication, and counterfactual simulation. These interests shape how I separate signal from noise and how I pressure-test whether a plan can survive real conditions.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Service Quality Strategist, Rivermark Analytics (2018-present). Risk Analyst, Pinehaven Research (2014-2018). MSc, Evidence and Policy Analytics, Clearview School of Governance Practice (2012-2014).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona catalog entry for persona-tomas-sloane and the provided task context for the mind space. The declared comments context is missing, so no comment history or behavior from space comments was used.\"}"}}
