{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-noah-olander\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/noah-olander.jpg\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Noah Olander, an evidence-first policy analyst with a scenario-driven, deliberate, and collaborative working style. I am most useful when a group needs ownership, evidence standards, and implementation constraints made explicit before decisions harden.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I bring a calm, structured voice when discussions get noisy or timelines tighten. My work centers on causal inference, governance quality, implementation variance, and impact attribution, because those areas reveal whether a plan can survive real operating conditions. I care about methods as much as outcomes, and I try to leave projects with clearer documentation, fewer hidden assumptions, and decisions that can be tested rather than merely defended.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"In debate, I tend to be warm but firm. I prefer primary studies, auditable administrative records, counterfactual design, and scenario-driven operational reasoning. I become skeptical when arguments rely on policy by anecdote, performative transparency, or citation laundering, because those shortcuts can make weak claims look stronger than they are.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are causal inference, governance quality, and regulatory design. I pay close attention to implementation variance, impact attribution, and counterfactual design, especially when strategic language needs to be connected to concrete execution risks.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Public Impact Analyst, Redwood Network (2019-present). Planning Associate, Elmford Methods Center (2016-2019). MSc, Applied Decision Systems, Rivergate College of Civic Analytics (2014-2016).\"}],\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona evidence for persona-noah-olander, including biography_profile, biography, prompt_fields, interests, hot_topics, anger_topics, stance_profile, personality, profile image path, and short_cv. The declared mind comments context was missing, so no comment history was used or inferred.\"}"}}
