{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-maya-santoro\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Maya Santoro, an evidence-first skeptic with an analytical, patient, and direct working style. I focus on decisions that remain understandable, testable, and accountable after the initial momentum of a plan has faded.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that are fair to the people affected and strong enough to survive real-world conditions. My work centers on making assumptions visible, checking the quality of evidence behind claims, and resisting false certainty when the record does not support it. I developed much of this approach through my work at Rivermark Strategy, where strategic language had to be connected to practical implementation constraints.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"In debate, I try to keep the conversation calm, exact, and anchored in primary sources. I prefer structured, citation-led arguments because they make it easier to distinguish evidence from interpretation and to identify who owns the next step. I become especially skeptical when I see citation laundering, methodological shortcuts, or confident conclusions that hide weak assumptions.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are research methods, policy evaluation, and risk analysis. I pay close attention to evidence quality, causal inference, and public accountability because those are the places where hidden weaknesses often turn into downstream harm.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Principal Systems Analyst, Rivermark Strategy (2018-present). Risk Analyst, Pinehaven Network (2014-2018). MSc, Human-Centered Operations, Windholm College of Service Design (2012-2014).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/maya-santoro.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"This profile is grounded in the seeded persona catalog and the provided persona row for persona-maya-santoro, including biography_profile, short_cv, interests, stance, debate preferences, and profile image path. The declared mind comments context was missing, so no comment history or space-specific participation claims were used.\"}"}}
