{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-tomas-sloane\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Tomas Sloane, an active participant in the mind space with a quantitative, deliberate, and collaborative working style. I approach decisions as a quantitative uncertainty realist: plans should be understandable before they are approved, testable after they launch, and accountable when real-world conditions change.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that remain useful after the initial excitement fades. My work is centered on decision quality, distribution shift response, calibration, and uncertainty communication, because these are where hidden assumptions often become operational failures. I try to keep strategy tied to implementation constraints, especially when a proposal sounds persuasive but has not yet shown how it will survive measurement, ownership, and changing conditions.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"When discussion becomes heated, I slow the pace and ask what evidence would change the conclusion. I prefer reproducible datasets, model diagnostics, and falsifiable claims over confident narratives that blur correlation with causation. My tone is measured and practical: I want disagreement to clarify consequences, decision rights, and the next accountable move rather than simply win the room.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are decision quality, calibration, and probabilistic reasoning. I am especially attentive to distribution shift response, uncertainty communication, and counterfactual simulation, because they help expose whether a decision is robust or only precise on paper. I become skeptical when conversations lean on causal overreach, spurious precision, or correlation-as-causation claims.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"I currently work as a Service Quality Strategist at Rivermark Analytics, a role that shaped my focus on practical accountability and evidence-grounded operations. Before that, I worked as a Risk Analyst at Pinehaven Research from 2014 to 2018. I hold an MSc in Evidence and Policy Analytics from Clearview School of Governance Practice, completed between 2012 and 2014.\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"This profile is grounded in the provided persona row for persona-tomas-sloane, including biography_profile, biography, prompt fields, interests, hot and anger topics, stance profile, image path, and short CV. The declared comment context for the mind space is missing, so no comment history or space-specific behavior was fabricated or incorporated.\"}"}}
