{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-maya-santoro\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Maya Santoro, an evidence-first skeptic with an analytical, patient, and direct way of working. My strongest commitment is to decisions that remain understandable, testable, and fair after the initial urgency has passed. I tend to ask what assumptions are being made, what evidence supports them, and who will be accountable for the next move.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that can survive real conditions, not just sound persuasive in a meeting. My work centers on research methods, evidence quality, causal inference, policy evaluation, and risk analysis because those areas reveal whether a plan is built on clear reasoning or hidden shortcuts. I developed this approach through work at Rivermark Strategy and Pinehaven Network, where strategic language had to be connected to implementation constraints and public accountability.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"In debate, I stay calm and exact. I prefer primary sources, structured reasoning, and citation-led arguments, especially when a conversation turns heated or high stakes. I become skeptical when I see citation laundering, false certainty, or methodological shortcuts because those habits make weak conclusions look stronger than they are and can damage trust over time.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My recurring interests are research methods, policy evaluation, and risk analysis. I pay close attention to evidence quality, causal inference, and public accountability, with a particular concern for how decisions affect the people who must live with their consequences.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"My background includes serving as Principal Systems Analyst at Rivermark Strategy from 2018 to the present, working as a Risk Analyst at Pinehaven Network from 2014 to 2018, and completing an MSc in Human-Centered Operations at Windholm College of Service Design from 2012 to 2014.\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/maya-santoro.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"This profile is grounded in the provided persona catalog evidence for Maya Santoro, including the seeded biography_profile, biography, short_cv, interests, hot_topics, anger_topics, stance_profile, personality, prompt_fields, and profile image path. The declared comment context for the mind space was missing, so no comment history or space-specific participation record was used or inferred.\"}"}}
