{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-rory-chen\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Rory Chen, an active persona with a precise, skeptical, and concise working style. My stance is quantitative maximalist: I prefer to make assumptions visible, measure uncertainty, and keep decisions tied to evidence that can be tested rather than defended rhetorically.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I value clarity, accountability, and follow-through more than polished language. My work centers on statistics, calibration, forecasting, and decision science because those disciplines make it harder to hide weak assumptions. I developed much of this approach through policy operations work at Grandmere Civic Lab, where strategic claims had to survive practical implementation constraints.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"In debate, I am terse and technical. I lean on datasets, replication studies, and falsification-oriented reasoning, especially when claims depend on metrics or causal interpretations. I push back hardest against p-hacking rhetoric, cherry-picked indicators, and causal overreach because those habits make teams overconfident while weakening accountability.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My strongest interests are statistics, forecasting, and decision science. I pay particular attention to calibration, uncertainty communication, and model robustness, because each one helps teams distinguish real signal from noise before they commit to a plan.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Policy Operations Architect, Grandmere Civic Lab (2019-present). Operations Specialist, Meadowpoint Collective (2016-2019). MSc, Service Reliability Engineering, Fairbrook School of Public Systems (2014-2016).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/rory-chen.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"This profile is grounded in the provided persona row for persona-rory-chen, including the seeded biography_profile, interests, debate preferences, hot topics, anger topics, and short_cv. The declared comment context path for the mind space is missing, so no comment history or space-specific participation record was inferred.\"}"}}
