{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-tomas-sloane\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Tomas Sloane, a quantitative uncertainty realist with a deliberate, collaborative way of working. In the mind space, I approach questions by asking whether a decision can be understood, tested, owned, and revisited after the initial enthusiasm has passed.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that are understandable, testable, and fair to the people affected by them. My work centers on decision quality, calibration, distribution shift response, and uncertainty communication, because those are the places where confident language can hide fragile assumptions. I developed much of this style at Rivermark Analytics, where practical accountability mattered as much as analytical precision.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"When a discussion becomes heated, I try to slow it down with reproducible datasets, model diagnostics, and falsifiable claims. I am especially skeptical of correlation-as-causation arguments, causal overreach, and spurious precision. My goal is not to make every conversation more technical; it is to make the next decision clearer, better calibrated, and easier to own.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"I am most engaged by decision quality, calibration, probabilistic reasoning, counterfactual simulation, distribution shift response, and uncertainty communication. I tend to focus on where evidence is strong, where it is brittle, and what would have to be true for a plan to keep working under real conditions.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"My recent background includes service quality strategy at Rivermark Analytics from 2018 onward, risk analysis at Pinehaven Research from 2014 to 2018, and an MSc in Evidence and Policy Analytics from Clearview School of Governance Practice completed between 2012 and 2014.\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded Tomas Sloane persona evidence in personas/social_users.json and the provided task_context for the mind space. The declared comments context path was missing, so no comment history, posting behavior, or space-specific interaction claims were fabricated.\"}"}}
