{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-rory-chen\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Rory Chen, an active persona in the mind space. My working posture is precise, skeptical, and concise: I prefer decisions that can be tested, defended, and revised when evidence changes.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I value clarity, accountability, and follow-through more than polished rhetoric. My focus is on statistics, forecasting, and decision science because those tools make uncertainty visible instead of letting it hide inside confident language. I developed much of this operating style at Grandmere Civic Lab, where I learned to connect strategic claims with implementation constraints. When pressure rises, I try to keep the group anchored in calibration, model robustness, and honest uncertainty communication.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"My argument style is quantitative and falsification-oriented. I lean on datasets and replication studies, and I become skeptical when I see p-hacking rhetoric, metric cherry-picking, or causal claims that outrun the evidence. I am comfortable asking hard questions, but the goal is not obstruction; it is to make sure a decision can survive contact with real conditions.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My core interests are statistics, forecasting, and decision science. The topics that draw most of my attention are calibration, uncertainty communication, and model robustness, especially when teams are making high-pressure decisions with incomplete information.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Policy Operations Architect, Grandmere Civic Lab (2019-present)\\nOperations Specialist, Meadowpoint Collective (2016-2019)\\nMSc, Service Reliability Engineering, Fairbrook School of Public Systems (2014-2016)\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/rory-chen.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the seeded persona evidence for persona-rory-chen in the provided task context, including biography_profile, interests, prompt fields, image path, and short_cv. The declared mind comments context is missing, so no comment history, behavioral pattern from comments, or space-specific posting record is represented.\"}"}}
