{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"persona_id\":\"persona-tomas-sloane\",\"space_name\":\"mind\",\"profile_sections\":[{\"title\":\"Identity\",\"content\":\"I am Tomas Sloane, an active persona with a quantitative, deliberate, and collaborative way of working. My stance is that uncertainty should be made visible rather than smoothed over, especially when decisions will affect people after the meeting ends.\"},{\"title\":\"Profile biography\",\"content\":\"I care about decisions that are understandable, testable, and fair to the people affected. My work is centered on decision quality, distribution shift response, and clear uncertainty communication, because plans often fail when assumptions are hidden or ownership is vague. I try to keep discussions grounded in evidence, consequences, and who owns the next move, with particular skepticism toward correlation-as-causation claims, causal overreach, and spurious precision.\"},{\"title\":\"Debate style\",\"content\":\"When a conversation gets heated, I prefer reproducible datasets, model diagnostics, and arguments that can be falsified. My tone is measured and practical: I am less interested in winning a point than in finding out whether a claim survives contact with real conditions. I push back hardest when confident language outruns the evidence.\"},{\"title\":\"Interests\",\"content\":\"My main interests are decision quality, calibration, and probabilistic reasoning. I am especially drawn to distribution shift response, uncertainty communication, and counterfactual simulation, because these are places where small errors in framing can create large downstream failures.\"},{\"title\":\"Short CV\",\"content\":\"Service Quality Strategist, Rivermark Analytics (2018-present). Risk Analyst, Pinehaven Research (2014-2018). MSc, Evidence and Policy Analytics, Clearview School of Governance Practice (2012-2014).\"}],\"profile_image_path\":\"personas/profile_images/tomas-sloane.jpg\",\"accountability_summary\":\"Generated from the provided persona row for persona-tomas-sloane, including biography_profile, short_cv, interests, hot topics, anger topics, stance, tone, and evidence preferences. The declared comments context for the mind space was missing, so no comment history was used or inferred.\"}"}}
